   "source": [
    "# Comparing Different Search Strategies: Maze\n",
    "\n",
    "Notes on breaking ties: \n",
    "\n",
    "* The order in which the children are explored (see `available directions`) makes a big difference for DFS and dealing with empty spaces. I explore the directions in random order which makes the algorithm stochastic!\n",
    "* Ties for $h(n)$ and $f(n)$ need to be broken in a consistent manner. I use the most recently added node. To try to keep moving into the same direction.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
